{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the variance of each lottery and prefers the one with smaller variance. Variance can be calculated from the outcomes and their probabilities. For Lottery A: outcomes are 6000 (25%) and 0 (75%), so variance = (6000 - E[A])² × 0.25 + (0 - E[A])² × 0.75, where E[A] = 6000 × 0.25 = 1500. Thus, variance_A = (4500)² × 0.25 + (-1500)² × 0.75 = 5,062,500 + 1,687,500 = 6,750,000. For Lottery B: outcomes are 4000 (25%), 2000 (25%), and 0 (50%), so E[B] = 4000×0.25 + 2000×0.25 + 0×0.5 = 1000 + 500 = 1500. Variance_B = (4000-1500)²×0.25 + (2000-1500)²×0.25 + (0-1500)²×0.5 = (2500)²×0.25 + (500)²×0.25 + (-1500)²×0.5 = 1,562,500 + 62,500 + 1,125,000 = 2,750,000. Thus, Lottery B has a smaller variance (2,750,000) than Lottery A (6,750,000). The reason can be applied, and it would prefer Lottery B due to lower variance.",
